    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The test tree has one runnable test class (plus the abstract base and helpers), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system, mapping points to a level and returning both fields.\n\n**Points logic** \u2014 `AssignMembershipLevel.java`: starts at 0, `+2` email present, `+1` `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` household of 3+ (`householdSize >= 3`), `+3` tenure over 365 days. Level is derived from points: `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+). It now sets both `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel`.\n\n**Supporting changes:**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added `membershipPoints` field (`membership_points` column) with getter/setter.\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 reordered the pipeline so `countHousehold` runs *before* `assignMembershipLevel`, since points now depend on `householdSize` (previously household was counted after).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema property and updated `membershipLevel` (max 1\u21924, new description) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries and serializes both fields.\n- DB schemas (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres `schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `membership_points` column; tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`.\n- `hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 appended a trailing `NULL` to the positional owners seed INSERTs to match the new column count (h2/postgres use named-column inserts, so unaffected).\n\nFor the test case (email present, no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure): 2 + 1 = **3 points \u2192 level 2**, matching the assertion.",
