    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners` (defined in `owners.POST.yml`), reading the code as it stands. The whole endpoint runs under one guard and one transaction, and every step is `govern: [ transaction ]`, so it all commits once at the end.\n\n**Gate (before any step)**\n- **Authorization:** `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"` \u2014 caller must have role `OWNER_ADMIN`.\n\n**Then, in pipeline order:**\n\n1. **NormalizeAddress** \u2014 *(side effect)* Binds the `@RequestBody` (the pipeline's single body-reading step) and rewrites `address` to canonical form (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations). Republishes the request as a variable for later steps. This normalized address is what the next validation and the identity/household logic see.\n\n2. **RequireOwnerFields** \u2014 *(validation)* Rejects if any mandatory field is blank/missing: `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`. Because address was already normalized, a blank-after-normalization address fails here \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.\n\n3. **RejectFutureRegistrationDate** \u2014 *(validation)* If `registrationDate` is supplied and later than the server's current date \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException`. Absent date is allowed.\n\n4. **ValidatePostcode** \u2014 *(validation)* `postcode` is optional. If present it must be exactly 4 digits; if the city maps to a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in that range. Otherwise \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (malformed or out-of-range).\n\n5. **NormalizeTelephone** \u2014 *(side effect + validation)* Rewrites `telephone` to E.164 (`+61\u2026`, strips separators, drops a leading national `0`, requires 8\u201315 digits). Unparseable \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n6. **NormalizeEmail** \u2014 *(side effect + validation)* `email` optional; if present, must match a basic syntactic pattern (else `InvalidEmailException`), then it's trimmed and lower-cased and written back.\n\n7. **RejectDisposableEmailDomain** \u2014 *(validation)* If the email's domain is on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException`.\n\n8. **RejectDuplicateOwner** \u2014 *(validation)* Household-duplicate block. Computes `HouseholdId` from `(lastName, postcode)`; if any existing owner shares it \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409). Bypassed when the request sets `sharesHousehold = true`.\n\n9. **RejectCityAtCapacity** \u2014 *(validation)* Counts existing owners in the same city (matched case-insensitively, whitespace-normalized); if \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n10. **RejectOverDailyLimit** \u2014 *(validation)* Computes the effective business day (supplied-or-today, rolled forward off weekends to Monday); if \u2265 100 existing owners already have that `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` (429).\n\n11. **BuildOwner** \u2014 *(side effect)* Maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`; defaults `registrationDate` to server date if absent, then applies the business-day (weekend\u2192Monday) adjustment and stores it.\n\n12. **AssignCustomerCode** \u2014 *(side effect)* Sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>`, where REGION comes from postcode/city (`Locality`, falling back to `UNKNOWN`) and HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n13. **AssignMembershipNumber** \u2014 *(side effect)* Sets `membershipNumber = <customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY being the last two digits of the registration year.\n\n14. **CountNamesakes** \u2014 *(side effect)* Sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n15. **CountHousehold** \u2014 *(side effect)* Sets `householdSize` = existing owners sharing the same `HouseholdId` plus this one.\n\n16. **AssignMembershipLevel** \u2014 *(side effect)* Computes `membershipPoints` (email +2, `namesakeCount==0` +1, `householdSize>=3` +2, tenure >365 days +3) and derives numeric `membershipLevel` (1: 0\u20131 pts, 2: 2\u20133, 3: 4\u20135, 4: \u22656).\n\n17. **FlagBulkSignup** \u2014 *(side effect)* Sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if more than 80 existing owners already share this registration day.\n\n18. **DetectPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 *(side effect)* If `sharesHousehold` is true \u2192 `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`. Otherwise, if the household id matches any existing owner \u2192 `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = the lowest matching owner id; else false/null.\n\n19. **SaveOwner** \u2014 *(side effect)* Persists the owner via `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.\n\n20. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 *(side effect)* Logs an audit line to the `AUDIT` logger with the new id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and `membershipLevel`.\n\n21. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 *(side effect)* Maps to `OwnerDto` and sends `201 Created` with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body.\n\n**Notes on ordering semantics**\n- Validations 2\u201310 all run *before* the entity is built/saved, and steps 8\u201310, 14, 15, 17, 18 use `ownerRepository.findAll()`, so they see only owners that existed *before* this create.\n- Because everything is under one transaction, any escalation thrown mid-pipeline rolls the whole thing back; the exception handlers in `officefloor/escalation/` map each exception to its status (400s for field/format validation, 409 for duplicate/city-capacity, 429 for daily limit)."
